# Cursor Cloud specific instructions

These notes apply only to Cursor Cloud agents (kept out of the shared `AGENTS.md` since T3 Code is
developed in many places). They cover this environment's toolchain and non-obvious run caveats.

## Toolchain

Login shells source `~/.config/vite-plus/env` from `~/.bashrc`. That puts Vite+ `vp` 1.4.0 (the
version in `pnpm-workspace.yaml`) and Node 26.12.1 (`package.json` `engines.node`) first on `PATH`.

- Node gotcha: `/exec-daemon/node` is Node 22 and wins in shells that do not source `~/.bashrc`.
  Run commands in a login shell (`bash -lc '...'`) or through `vp`, which uses the managed Node.
- `vp` is the package manager and task runner (`vp i`, `vp test run <files>`, `vp run dev`,
  `vp run --filter <pkg> <script>`). `vpr` is the `vp run` shortcut.
- Rust stable is on `PATH` via rustup. Crates under `native/` use edition 2024, so rustc must be
  1.85 or newer. `cargo test --locked --manifest-path native/resource-monitor/Cargo.toml` is the
  small native check.
- Linux native modules (`node-pty`) and the desktop secret helper need the C toolchain,
  pkg-config, and libsecret headers. ImageMagick is installed for Linux desktop artifact builds.
- Playwright's headless Chromium shell is installed for web and server browser tests.

## Running the web app

- `vp run dev` from the repo root starts the server and the Vite web app together. Read the ports
  and the pairing URL from stdout (`pairingUrl:`). Do not set `VITE_HTTP_URL` or `VITE_WS_URL`.
- Open that pairing URL before the web UI can talk to the server. The bare origin does not
  authenticate a new browser.
- This checkout's dev runner uses `~/.t3` as its base directory. Never point a server at a
  developer's live `~/.t3/userdata`. On a Cloud Agent VM, `~/.t3` is that VM's own state.
- A missing provider CLI does not stop the server. Codex logs an error when `codex` is not on
  `PATH`, and the model picker can show no models until a provider is available. Claude's health
  check logs a warning when `claude` is not installed. `vp run dev` is expected to register the
  free `Replay (dev)` provider for turn streams that should not call a paid model.
- Avoid production `build` / `start` for day-to-day work.

## Android

The Android SDK is not installed here, and this VM has no `/dev/kvm`, so an emulator will not
run. Mobile native builds are out of scope. Typecheck and `vp run lint:mobile` still apply to
`apps/mobile` changes.

## Known flaky tests (unrelated to setup)

- `apps/server/src/git/GitManager.test.ts` (cross-repo PR metadata, can time out at 12s).
- `apps/server/src/provider/ProviderRegistry.test.ts` (codex binaryPath re-probe ordering).
